<title>FRANCE: Galeries Lafayette H1 oper loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Galeries Lafayette H1 oper loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating			     loss   137  vs     loss  246</p>
<p>    Pre-tax				profit  390  vs     loss  282</p>
<p>    Exceptional			   gain   526  vs    charge   4</p>
<p>    Financial expense			    105  vs	     132</p>
<p>    Turnover				    13,698  vs	  13,802</p>
<p>NOTE - Galeries Lafayette reported its first-half results in a financial advertisement.</p>
<p>It said 104 million francs of the 109 million improvement in operating profit came from its big stores division, and the drop in financial expense was due to lower interest rates.</p>
<p>The exceptional gain was largely due to the sale-leaseback by its SOGEFIN unit of a complex in Nice for 750 million francs. More such operations have occurred since July 1, generating 260 million francs, and others are under negotiation and are expected to reinforce the balance sheet by more than one billion francs, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
